From: ROCKNIX
Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: stop a userspace disconnect double-releasing the BSS

003 fixed the double release on the shutdown path, but the same fault is
reachable from an ordinary userspace disconnect, with no poweroff involved.
`nmcli device disconnect wlan1` is enough to take the board down:

  Internal error: Oops: 0000000096000021 [#1] SMP
  RTW: netdev_vir_if_close(wlan1) , bup=1
  Workqueue: cfg80211 cfg80211_event_work
  pc : cfg80211_unhold_bss+0x2c/0xa0
  lr : cfg80211_wdev_release_bsses+0x38/0xc0
  x19: 0000000000000000

x19 is the BSS being released and it is NULL, because a previous release
already cleared it.

cfg80211 handles a userspace-requested disconnect itself: it tears the
connection down and releases the BSSes synchronously before returning from
the ioctl. The driver then indicates the disconnect a second time from its
own mlme, that indication is queued with GFP_ATOMIC, and when
cfg80211_event_work runs it enters cfg80211_wdev_release_bsses() again for a
wdev whose BSSes are already gone.

The driver already has the machinery to suppress this -- cfg80211_rtw_disconnect()
sets not_indic_disco around _rtw_disconnect() -- but the whole block is
compiled out unless RTW_CFG80211_BLOCK_DISCON_WHEN_DISCONNECT is set, and it
is cleared for every kernel >= 4.2. That was presumably safe when cfg80211
tolerated the redundant event; since the wdev->links[] rework it is not. The
pre-4.2 default is the correct one here, so restore it for kernels carrying
links[].

The second hunk fixes a porting error with the same end effect. valid_links
is the MLO link bitmap and is 0 for an ordinary non-MLO connection, which
still uses links[0]. Gating the current_bss teardown on it means the branch
never runs, so rtw_wdev_unregister() leaves current_bss set on a wdev that is
going away -- the pre-5.19 code it replaced (`if (wdev->current_bss)`) had no
such condition. Dropping valid_links from the test restores that behaviour;
the current_bss check on its own is still enough to keep it from firing when
cfg80211 has already done the release.

Reproduced and confirmed on a Miyoo Flip running 7.0.2: without this, three
disconnect cycles never complete the first one. Note the failure is
self-sustaining -- once the oops kills the cfg80211_event_work thread, the
module can no longer be unloaded (rmmod blocks forever and the refcount goes
to -1), so the board has to be rebooted.

--- a/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.h
+++ b/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.h
@@ -19,7 +19,16 @@
 #define RTW_CFG80211_BLOCK_DISCON_WHEN_DISCONNECT	BIT1
 
 #ifndef RTW_CFG80211_BLOCK_STA_DISCON_EVENT
-#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(4, 2, 0))
+/* WHEN_DISCONNECT was dropped for >= 4.2 on the assumption that cfg80211
+ * tolerates the driver posting its own disconnect on top of the one it is
+ * already processing for a userspace-requested disconnect. Since the
+ * wdev->links[] rework it does not: both indications reach
+ * cfg80211_wdev_release_bsses() and the second one releases a BSS the first
+ * already dropped, so cfg80211_put_bss() faults and the machine panics on
+ * every nmcli disconnect. Keep the pre-4.2 behaviour on kernels that have
+ * links[].
+ */
+#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(4, 2, 0)) && (LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(5, 19, 2))
 #define RTW_CFG80211_BLOCK_STA_DISCON_EVENT (RTW_CFG80211_BLOCK_DISCON_WHEN_CONNECT)
 #else
 #define RTW_CFG80211_BLOCK_STA_DISCON_EVENT (RTW_CFG80211_BLOCK_DISCON_WHEN_CONNECT | RTW_CFG80211_BLOCK_DISCON_WHEN_DISCONNECT)
--- a/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c
+++ b/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c
@@ -11180,7 +11180,12 @@
 
 	#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 11, 0)) || defined(COMPAT_KERNEL_RELEASE)
 	#if (defined(CONFIG_ACK_5_15_LTS_KERNEL) || (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(5, 19, 2)))
-	if (wdev->valid_links && wdev->links[0].client.current_bss)
+	/* valid_links is the MLO link bitmap and stays 0 for an ordinary
+	 * connection, which link 0 is still used for. Requiring it here meant the
+	 * branch never ran and current_bss was left set on a wdev about to go
+	 * away, unlike the pre-5.19 code this replaced.
+	 */
+	if (wdev->links[0].client.current_bss)
 	#else
 	if (wdev->current_bss)
 	#endif
